    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0159" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg85"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 1, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose for the
                    information of his excellency, Viscount Monck, a copy of a communication of the
                    25th ultimo from M._______, <pb facs="0160" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/> esquire, of
                    Cincinnati, Ohio, indicating parties who would be likely to give important
                    evidence in regard to the plots and hostile expeditions in Canada against the
                    peace of the United States.</p>
                <p>I must request that the name of the person furnishing the information may be
                    regarded as confidential.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
